        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d3d2b409-08b0-5b09-af20-d48cad363c37",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Ox-tongue pastry, Youtiao\n- Concepts: Fried dough foods, pastry shapes, alternate names\n\nFacts:\n- Ox-tongue pastry is a fried dough food that is elliptical in shape and resembles an ox tongue or a horse ear.\n- Youtiao is a long, golden-brown, deep-fried strip of dough eaten in China and in other East and Southeast Asian cuisines.\n- Youtiao is also known as Chinese fried churros, Chinese cruller, Chinese oil stick, Chinese doughnut, fried breadstick, and You Char Kway, Cakwe, Cakoi, Kueh, or Kuay in Malaysia, Indonesia, and Singapore.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
